        <initializer>= false</initializer>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Is this value an IMPLICIT_DEF that can be erased? </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>IMPLICIT_DEF values should only exist at the end of a basic block that is a predecessor to a phi-value. These IMPLICIT_DEF instructions can be safely erased if they are overlapping a live value in the other live interval.</para>
<para>Weird control flow graphs and incomplete PHI handling in ProcessImplicitDefs can very rarely create IMPLICIT_DEF values with longer live ranges. Such IMPLICIT_DEF values should be treated like normal values. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
